From: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 20:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] AP MLD: advertise a TID-to-link mapping

Depends on 608-AP-MLD-end-the-Critical-Update-flag-at-the-DTIM-Beac.patch
and on the mac80211 patches that add NL80211_CMD_ADV_TTLM_REQUEST and
NL80211_EXT_FEATURE_AP_ADV_TTLM.

hostapd has no way to advertise a TID-to-link mapping of an AP MLD
(IEEE 802.11be-2024, 35.3.7.2.4). Only CONFIG_TESTING_OPTIONS adds a
TID-To-Link Mapping element, without the Mapping Switch Time and the
Expected Duration fields that an advertised mapping needs.

Add hostapd_adv_ttlm_request(), which asks a driver that declares
NL80211_EXT_FEATURE_AP_ADV_TTLM and
NL80211_EXT_FEATURE_BEACON_CRIT_UPDATE to map all TIDs to a subset of
the links of the AP MLD for a duration. The driver times the switch and
the end and reports each step with the cookie of the request, so that
hostapd ignores the events of an earlier mapping. Once the driver
reports the start on a link, the Beacon and Probe Response frames of
that link carry the element with the Mapping Switch Time of the link
and the full Expected Duration. Once the mapping is established, the
element drops the Mapping Switch Time and carries the remaining
Expected Duration, and the Reduced Neighbor Report sets the Disabled
Link Indication of each disabled link. At the end the element leaves
the frames.

(Re)Association Response frames carry the element only once the mapping
is established, as only Beacon and Probe Response frames carry the
Mapping Switch Time field (9.4.2.324). The remaining Expected Duration
counts from the TBTT of a Beacon frame and from the most recent TBTT for
other frames. hostapd sees no TBTT, so it takes the CLOCK_BOOTTIME of the
establishment and of a TBTT of each link from the events of the driver.
Without them, the TBTTs count from the event of the establishment.

An affiliated AP that becomes disabled or enabled through the mapping
sets the Critical Update flag (35.3.10). Start a critical update on each
link at both steps; the driver ends it at the DTIM Beacon. A request
fails if a link is a nontransmitted BSSID, whose flag the driver does
not end. The BSS Parameters Change Count stays: 9.4.2.169.2 increments
it for the critical updates of 11.2.3.14 alone, which name no
advertised mapping. Notify ubus of the establishment and of the end.

Without a given switch time, the mapping is established two DTIM
intervals after the request, so that each associated non-AP MLD in
power save receives a DTIM Beacon with the element before the switch.
The switch time is at most 0xffff TUs, the range of the Mapping Switch
Time field.

cfg80211 ends the mapping when a link of the AP MLD stops, so hostapd
ends it as well when it stops a link, and updates the frames of the
other links. Both a mapping and a link removal change the links of the
AP MLD, so hostapd rejects a link removal while a mapping is requested
or established, and a request while a link removal runs.

The length of the element covers the largest element while a mapping
is advertised, since its presence depends on the frame subtype and on
the time of the write.

Signed-off-by: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
---
--- a/src/ap/ap_drv_ops.c
+++ b/src/ap/ap_drv_ops.c
@@ -590,6 +590,17 @@ int hostapd_if_link_remove(struct hostap
 	return hapd->driver->link_remove(hapd->drv_priv, type, ifname,
 					 hapd->mld_link_id);
 }
+
+
+int hostapd_drv_adv_ttlm_request(struct hostapd_data *hapd, u16 links,
+				 u32 switch_time, u32 duration, u64 *cookie)
+{
+	if (!hapd->driver || !hapd->drv_priv || !hapd->driver->adv_ttlm_request)
+		return -EOPNOTSUPP;
+
+	return hapd->driver->adv_ttlm_request(hapd->drv_priv, links,
+					      switch_time, duration, cookie);
+}
 #endif /* CONFIG_IEEE80211BE */
 
 
